        "date": "2026-11-13T10:07:44Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): Explain G-code option, explain() PRELUDE helper, manifest and refusal\n\nAdds the opt-in Explain G-code post option (PostOptions.explain, per\ndocument and per setup, through the existing undoable post-options\ncommands; the project file writes an `explain` key only when on). The\nscript engine loads an explain() helper after the PRELUDE and arms it\nonly when the option is on and the post's manifest states\n`explains = \"paren\" | \"semi\"` (optional `commentMax`, 8..=255, default\n60). Unarmed, explain() returns \"\", so Explain-off output is unchanged.\nExplain on with a post that states no form is refused by the post's\nname before any hook runs.\n\nFixes #1386\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
